{"chapters":[{"title":"Scan the key's history","code":"class TimeMap:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.store = defaultdict(list)\n\n    def set(self, key, value, timestamp):\n        self.store[key].append((timestamp, value))\n\n    def get(self, key, timestamp):\n        for t, v in reversed(self.store[key]):\n            if t <= timestamp:\n                return v\n        return \"\"","frames":[{"caption":"<strong>Scan the key's history</strong> &mdash; set O(1), get O(n) time, O(n) extra space. Running <code>tm = TimeMap(); tm.set(\"foo\", \"bar\", 1); assert tm.get(\"foo\", 1) == \"bar\" and tm.get(\"foo\", 3) == \"bar\"; tm.set(\"foo\", \"bar2\", 4) …</code>. Step through to watch the code work on this input.","line":2,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self","label":"self","v":["T","i","m","e","M","a","p"],"cls":["","","","","","",""]}],"vars":[["self","'TimeMap'",0]],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>self.store = defaultdict(list)</code> &mdash; returns <code>None</code>; <code>self.store = {}</code>","line":3,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.store","label":"self.store (defaultdict)","v":[],"cls":[],"keys":[]}],"vars":[],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>self.store[key].append((timestamp, value))</code> &mdash; returns <code>None</code>; <code>self.store['foo'] = [(1, 'bar')]</code>; <code>key = 'foo'</code>; <code>value = 'bar'</code>; <code>timestamp = 1</code>","line":6,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.store","label":"self.store (defaultdict)","v":["[(1, '…"],"cls":["cur"],"keys":["foo"]}],"vars":[["key","'foo'",1],["value","'bar'",1],["timestamp","1",1]],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>for t, v in reversed(self.store[key]):</code> &mdash; <code>t = 1</code>; <code>v = 'bar'</code>","line":9,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.store","label":"self.store (defaultdict)","v":["[(1, '…"],"cls":[""],"keys":["foo"]}],"vars":[["key","'foo'",0],["timestamp","1",0],["t","1",1],["v","'bar'",1]],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>if t &lt;= timestamp:</code> &rarr; <strong>true</strong> 