. <strong>Result: ''</strong>","line":12,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.store","label":"self.store (defaultdict)","v":["[(1, '…","[]"],"cls":["",""],"keys":["foo","nope"]}],"vars":[["key","'nope'",0],["timestamp","10",0]],"stack":[]}]},{"title":"Binary search each key's sorted timestamps","code":"class TimeMap:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.times = defaultdict(list)\n        self.values = defaultdict(list)\n\n    def set(self, key, value, timestamp):\n        self.times[key].append(timestamp)       # arrives in increasing order\n        self.values[key].append(value)\n\n    def get(self, key, timestamp):\n        i = bisect.bisect_right(self.times[key], timestamp) - 1\n        return self.values[key][i] if i >= 0 else \"\"","frames":[{"caption":"<strong>Binary search each key's sorted timestamps</strong> &mdash; set O(1), get O(log n) time, O(n) extra space. Running <code>tm = TimeMap(); tm.set(\"foo\", \"bar\", 1); assert tm.get(\"foo\", 1) == \"bar\" and tm.get(\"foo\", 3) == \"bar\"; tm.set(\"foo\", \"bar2\", 4) …</code>. Step through to watch the code work on this input.","line":2,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self","label":"self","v":["T","i","m","e","M","a","p"],"cls":["","","","","","",""]}],"vars":[["self","'TimeMap'",0]],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>self.times = defaultdict(list)</code> &mdash; <code>self.times = {}</code>","line":3,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.times","label":"self.times (defaultdict)","v":[],"cls":[],"keys":[]}],"vars":[],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>self.values = defaultdict(list)</code> &mdash; returns <code>None</code>; <code>self.values = {}</code>","line":4,"panels":[{"t":"arr","id":"self.times","label":"self.times (defaultdict)","v":[],"cls":[],"keys":[]},{"t":"arr","id":"self.values","label":"self.values (defaultdict)","v":[],"cls":[],"keys":[]}],"vars":[],"stack":[]},{"caption":"<code>self.times[key].append(timestamp)</code> &mdash; <code>self.times['foo'] = [1]</code>; <code>key = 'foo'</code>; <code>value = 'bar'</cod